@model BuryChoice.Models.MainViewModel


@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home Page";
}

<section class="container">
    <div class="columns p-5">
        <div class="column">
            <div class="content">
                <h2>What is this website?</h2>

                Decisions are hard, especially when picking your child's high school. This website aims to try and help.
                The following are questions to consider
                <ul>
                    <li>Is the school academically what I'd want?</li>
                    <li>After high school, where to the children go?</li>
                    <li>What are my chances of getting accepted at the school?</li>
                    <li>How does the school feel? Vibes, layout, size, feel.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="container">
    <div class="columns p-5">
        <div class="column">
            <div class="content">
                <h2>Academia</h2>

                <p> The Department for Education (DfE) has a website dedicated to comparing school and college performance (CSCP) and will quite happily show comparison tables for the whole of Bury <a href="https://www.compare-school-performance.service.gov.uk/schools-by-type?step=default&table=schools&region=351&geographic=la&for=secondary" rel="nofollow">Compare school and college performance for Bury</a></p>

                <p>The DfE has a number of measurements that schools can be held accountable against</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Attainment 8 - Overall average score for 8 top subjects for the school include English, Maths, Science, History, Geography, Foreign languages (and others). <i>Effectively most of the subjects your child will take in year 10 averaged together.</i></li>
                    <li>Grade 5 and Above in English and Maths - Scored from 1 - 9 in English Literature/Language and Maths. 5 is the equivalent of a C, or low B.</li>
                    <li>Grade 4 and Above in English and Maths - Scored from 1 - 9 in English Literature/Language and Maths. 4 is a C</li>
                    <li>Percentage staying in education, employment, or apprenticeship</li>
                </ul>

                <p>Each of the above can be divided up into areas, such as from Disadvantaged backgrounds, or English as an Additional Language (EAL), however these are not in scope here. They are covered on <a href="https://www.compare-school-performance.service.gov.uk/">CSCP</a> or available in <a href="https://explore-education-statistics.service.gov.uk/find-statistics/key-stage-4-performance/2024-25">Explore Education Statistics (EES)</a></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>


<section class="container">
